# Knowledge → Markdown (mandatory)

Any **new durable fact** about this framework or an as-is pack (policy, structure, ownership, ops path, contract, lesson learned) must be written to a **`.md` file in the repo** in the **same session** it was discovered — before closing the task.

Chat replies and Cursor rules are **not** durable documentation.

## Where to write

| Knowledge type | Prefer |
| --- | --- |
| Standard methodology | Existing file under `docs/en/` (mirror `docs/pt-BR/` when bilingual) |
| As-is Loft pack | `docs/en/loft-infra/`, `docs/en/aiops-apps/` (+ pt-BR) |
| Templates / examples | `docs/en/templates/`, `examples/` |
| Framework adoption / index | Root `README.md` / `README.pt-BR.md`, `docs/en/README.md` |
| Deferred work | Register as [documentation debt](docs/en/documentation-debt.md) (owner, priority, status) |

**Confluence:** GitHub/local Markdown is the source of truth. Publish with `docs-sync/` only when needed (optional). Dual-surface link rules: [docs/en/publishing-surfaces.md](docs/en/publishing-surfaces.md). Never treat the Confluence UI as the only place of record.

## `.md` vs `.mdc` vs skill

| Artifact | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| **`.md`** | Durable knowledge for humans and agents |
| **`.mdc`** | Short agent guardrails — not a runbook substitute |
| **Skill** | Workflow for syncing docs after changes |

If a fact landed in a rule during a session, **mirror it into the appropriate `.md`** and keep the rule as a pointer.

## Checklist (before closing)

- [ ] New fact is in a `.md` file, not only in chat
- [ ] Existing canonical doc preferred over a new file
- [ ] Bilingual update when this repo requires EN + pt-BR
- [ ] Clear language (`docs-clear-language.mdc`)
- [ ] Debt registered if docs intentionally lag

## Anti-patterns

- Closing a session with discoveries only in the chat transcript
- Duplicating long runbooks inside `.mdc` files
- Editing Confluence without updating the repo Markdown source
